{{Term/Store|Selmie's Spot||Series, BotW, TotK}},{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK}}<ref>{{Cite|'''Selmie's Spot'''|Map|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|'''Selmie's Spot'''|Map|TotK}}</ref> also known as the '''Lodge on the Summit''',{{Exp Game|TotK}}<ref>{{Cite|Say what?! You rescued Teach from the back of that cave?! Then what are we doing standing around here?! I gotta get back to the {{Color TotK|Red|lodge on the summit}}! I bet Teach would want to thank you too, so you're welcome to come with!|Fin|TotK}}</ref> is a recurring location in {{TLoZ Series}}.

==Features and Overview==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Selmie's Spot is a small cabin located on the northern side of the [[Hebra East Summit]] in the [[Hebra Mountains]]. [[Shada Naw Shrine]] is located in a small cave nearby. Following her retirement from [[Shield Surfing]], [[Selmie]] took up residence in the cabin, supposedly waiting for a worthy opponent to come find her.<ref>{{Cite|Dude, apparently she's just waiting up on the {{Color BotW|Blue|Hebra Mountains}} for a worthy {{Color BotW|Red|shield-surfing}} opponent!|Baumar|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Dude, I heard the legendary {{Color BotW|Red|shield-surfer}} {{Color BotW|Blue|Selmie}} is just waiting on the {{Color BotW|Blue|Hebra Mountains}} for a worthy opponent!|Baumar|BotW}}</ref> The walls of the [[House]] are decorated with a variety of [[Shield]]s, and a [[Cooking Pot]] can be found over its fireplace. [[Link]] is also able to sleep in the cabin's [[Bed]] to restore his [[Heart]]s.<ref>{{Cite|Sleep until...|N/A|BotW}}</ref> Two [[Wooden Box]]es, which can be broken open for [[Material]]s, have been placed behind the cabin. Since it is located in a [[Freezing Climate]], Link requires at least two levels of Cold Resistance to visit Selmie's Spot without taking damage.

From Selmie's Spot, Selmie operates the [[Shield-Surfing (Mini-Game)|Shield-Surfing]] [[Mini-Game]].<ref>{{Cite|But if you don't mind a few pointers from a has-been, I'd be happy to critique your technique.|Selmie|BotW}}</ref> She charges Link 20 [[Rupee]]s per run.<ref>{{Cite|How does... Hmmm... Is {{Color BotW|Red|20 rupees}} a session OK with you?|Selmie|BotW}}</ref> After Link completes the beginner course, Selmie allows him to take on the advanced course.<ref>{{Cite|I'd like to see what you can do on a harder slope now. You can consider the {{Color BotW|Red|advanced course}} open for business!|Selmie|BotW}}</ref> As a reward for completing the advanced course, Selmie gifts Link the Shields that she has hung on her walls.<ref>{{Cite|Once you clear the advanced course, you can earn special shields for beating certain times. How's that for incentive?|Selmie|BotW}}</ref>

